<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">United National Independence Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1959–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as UNIP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United National Independence Party (UNIP) is a Zambian political party founded in 1959 and led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-kaunda">Kenneth Kaunda</a>, successor to the banned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a>. It led the campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> and won the elections of 1964 that brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> to independence as Zambia. It was the only legal party from 1972 to 1990 and lost power in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-national-independence-party.jpg" alt="United National Independence Party" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United National Independence Party · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unip-logo-torch-white-bg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
